d substring set MUST include `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` (the claim) AND `Lease.Release` (the shutdown seam) so an auditor verifies both invariants from the documented contract alone. Forward-applicable to ANY future worker-verification story whose invariant has a "hot path concurrency × shutdown safety" dual: BE-0386 (fake Dokploy contract tests can mirror this exclusivity × fault-injection pattern). (3) `VERIFY.SH RENUMBER OF OPTIONALS BLOCK CONTINUES` — inserting required step #11 between #10 (quota concurrency) and the optionals renumbered 11→12/12→13/13→14/14→15 in the same edit (govulncheck/staticcheck/golangci-lint/goreleaser). The static test pins `# 11. Required: job worker lease tests` but NOT the optional headers — those shift on every required insertion. Established by BE-0380's renumber pattern; this is now SIX consecutive required-step insertions (#6→#11) with optional renumbering, suggesting the next contributor adding a required step #12 (BE-0386 fake Dokploy) should follow the same edit shape: insert the new `# 12. Required` block AND renumber the four optional headers in the same Edit call. Per-story knobs for siblings: (a) canonical command (BE-0385 uses `go test -run TestJobWorkerLease ./...` filter-narrowed; BE-0386 will use `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`), (b) dedicated CI step name (BE-0385: "Job worker lease tests"), (c) verify.sh numeric prefix (next number after the last required step; renumber trailing optionals in the same edit), (d) SECURITY.md section heading and substring set (per-suite invariants; preserve the closed-set discipline so the matcher fails loudly), (e) AGENTS.md subsection (mirrors the SECURITY.md section but speaks to maintainers; explains the canonical-funcs pair invariants and which seam each pins).
